(KEY-22 — `Pivot` starts `pivot_root(2)`. The statement is compiled but
 deliberately NOT executed: a successful pivot would replace the root
 filesystem of whoever ran the probe. The guard is a runtime-false boolean,
 so the compiler still parses and lowers the statement.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox KEY-22.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   pivot compiled, not executed
)
a boolean called 'the root should move' is false.
If 'the root should move' then,
    Pivot root to "/newroot" with old root "/newroot/oldroot".
Print "pivot compiled, not executed".
